## Build locally

Requirements: JDK 17, Android SDK (cmdline-tools or Android Studio).

```bash
./gradlew assembleRelease
```

The signed APK lands in `app/build/outputs/apk/release/`.

## Build in CI (no local Android SDK needed)

This project includes `.github/workflows/build.yml`. Push to GitHub and the
APK is built as a workflow artifact.

## Customize

- App name, URL, colors, package id: edit `webview.json` at the repo root,
  then re-run `webview build --kotlin --output .` to regenerate.
- Icon: replace `app/src/main/res/mipmap-*/ic_launcher.png` (or set `icon`
  in `webview.json` to a source PNG and regenerate).
- Signing: replace the debug signing config in `app/build.gradle.kts` with
  your own keystore before publishing to the Play Store.

## What it does

- Loads {{ url }} in a hardware-accelerated Android `WebView`.
- Off-domain links {{ "stay in the app" if allow_external_links else "open in the user's real browser" }}.
- Pull-to-refresh.
- `tel:`, `mailto:`, `sms:` links → system handler.
- Splash screen via the AndroidX SplashScreen API.
- Edge-to-edge layout, system bar tinting.
- Saves & restores WebView state across rotations.
- App-link intent filter for `https://{{ host }}/*`.

